date,os,session,session_name,session_id,cloud_session_id,method,check_required,host,mux,cwd,config,note
日期,作業系統,session,Claude session 名稱,session 識別碼,雲端 session id,送達方式,需要檢查,主機,multiplexer,專案目錄,設定檔,備註
2026-09-09,macos,Swift-Cross-UI-Mac,Swift-Cross-UI-Mac,6c91a77a-086e-49d5-ad35-2d615900505e,session_01JYeEdTTK6beUhKUzevGa3S,session-id,no,local,screen,/Volumes/Windows/proj_Win/swift-cross-ui,,"This Mac. session_id is this very session (its transcript is ~/.claude/projects/-Volumes-Windows-proj-Win-swift-cross-ui/6c91a77a-....jsonl). **A session-id beat is not the same act as a mux beat, and the difference is worth knowing before arming it**: claude -p -r <id> appends a HEADLESS turn to that conversation and returns the reply to this script, whereas the mux route types into a live terminal where a human can see it. Measured 2026-09-09 on a throwaway session: claude -p -r <id> ""Are you still working ?"" returned the same session_id and the reply Yes, I am here and ready to help"
2026-09-09,windows,Swift-Cross-UI-Windows,Swift-Cross-UI-Windows,40ac6c86-ec5f-43e2-9851-ea99a1ad2983,session_01UhzCvvTNBk8UTaSsmBikAQ,session-id,yes,winnode,tmux,~/proj/swift-cross-ui,~/.multissh/generated/config2Win,"Windows-native claude, reached with multissh exec plus claude -p -r <session_id>. **session_id is the LOCAL uuid and that is the one claude -r eats** -- it is the filename of ~/.claude/projects/<proj>/<uuid>.jsonl. cloud_session_id is the claude.ai/code/<id> form that appears in commit trailers and is NOT accepted by -r; both are kept because a row carrying only the cloud id would look addressable and would not be. No multiplexer is involved on this route and none is needed, which matters because this machine has no tmux, no screen and no pacman to install either. Measured 2026-09-09 through multissh -F config2Win winnode: claude is at /c/Users/lowei/AppData/Local/Microsoft/WinGet/Links/claude and reports 2.1.216"
